// v6.8 (30 Jul 2026): PER-TOKEN PA BADGES (Jay: "the PA grid too — all ~17 tokens", after
//   choosing this over the smaller "single ticks only" option, aware it's the bigger,
//   riskier restructure). Table widened 2 -> 18 columns (PA_LAST_COL=17): col0=label,
//   cols1-17=one cell per PA pattern token. A fired token gets its own dark-navy/white
//   badge (C_BADGE_BG/C_BADGE_TXT, identical to the constants ported into Weinstein the
//   same session, so a fired token reads the same colour in both panels); an unfired one
//   blends into the row's own soft-pastel bg. Built from two arrays + one loop rather than
//   17 hardcoded cells — a Pine loop's COMPILED size is fixed by its body, not by how many
//   times it runs, so the loop is cheap; the loop naturally covers the bull path's 17
//   tokens and the recovery path's 10, the unused tail columns render blank.
//   Every OTHER row (all ~24 f_row rows + header/TRIGGER/STATUS/VERDICT) now merges
//   col1..17 so it still reads as a plain 2-column row — the width change is invisible
//   everywhere except the PA row itself.
//   Made the 30-Jul width fix's PA-grid `\n` split MOOT (each token has its own cell now,
//   nothing to wrap) — left as a comment marker only, not re-litigated.
//   f_it() is DELETED, not retired: its only 27 callers were the _g0..g4 concatenation
//   lines, all replaced by the array/loop version above.
//   ⚠ TOKEN-CEILING RISK, stated plainly: this is the largest single addition to this
//   file since the CONTEXT ROW that overshot the ~100,256 compile-token limit and had to
//   be reverted (v6.4/v6.5, same day). This change is architecturally different — most of
//   its size is the merge_cells calls added to ~28 existing rows plus 34 array.push calls,
//   not dense new logic — but headroom was NOT re-measured before writing it. Real chance
//   this does not compile on the first try.
//
// v6.7 (30 Jul 2026): COLUMN ALIGNMENT + THE PANEL-WIDTH FIX THAT ACTUALLY WORKS (Jay).
//   1. Both columns now hug the CENTRE divider — label right-aligned, value left-aligned
//      — instead of each hugging its own outer edge (which left a dead gap down the
//      middle of every row). Applied to f_row (all ~24 rows) and the four direct-cell
//      rows (header, TRIGGER, PA-header, STATUS, VERDICT).
//   2. "You tried wrapping VERDICT to shrink the panel, it didn't work — try again."
//      Root cause: Pine sizes a COLUMN to the widest SINGLE UNBROKEN line across EVERY
//      cell in it, not just the one row you edit. VERDICT was already wrapped into 4
//      lines, but several OTHER things were still one very long unbroken line and kept
//      setting the column width regardless: the PA condition grid (17 tokens, one line
//      — the actual worst offender, wider than any wrapped Verdict line), the Plan row
//      (entry-method + SL + T1 + T2 all concatenated), and roughly eight of the Verdict
//      branches' OWN L1-L5 strings (each one is "wrapped" only in the sense of being one
//      of four lines — several of those four were themselves 120-170 char unbroken
//      strings). Added internal `\n` breaks to the PA grid (split after the 3rd group),
//      the Plan row (method above, SL/T1/T2 below), and every verdict branch string over
//      ~100 chars, at its natural clause boundary. `\n` inside a string literal costs
//      ZERO compiled tokens either way, same as the v5.9 discovery that a comment does.
//
// v6.6 (30 Jul 2026): SOFT PANEL PALETTE (Jay, comparing to the Weinstein & Swing Pro
//   Dashboard panel screenshot: "more soft on my eyes and easy to read"). S4 rendered
//   neon/bright TEXT on a near-black row background; Weinstein renders a solid pastel
//   BACKGROUND per row with dark text — the background does the signalling, not a
//   glowing foreground. New f_softBg(color) buckets a semantic colour by its dominant
//   RGB channel (blue/orange/green/red/gray) into one of five fixed pastels; f_row now
//   applies it + one dark text constant (C_SOFTTXT) to BOTH cells of every row, so all
//   ~50 existing call sites get the new look with zero change at the call site. The
//   TRIGGER / PA-header / STATUS / VERDICT rows (built with direct table.cell, not
//   f_row) got the same treatment individually. Known simplification: #7b1fa2 (the
//   pa_col_v "strong Σ" purple) buckets into the blue pastel rather than getting its
//   own hue — acceptable, not a bug, kept for token cost.
//   Version jumps v6.3 -> v6.6: v6.4/v6.5 were a CONTEXT ROW (Stage/RRG/RS/trend/RSI)
//   that overshot the compile-token ceiling and was fully reverted the same day — those
//   numbers exist only in git history, not in this file. Numbering resumes past them so
